For vial cultures, dissolve all compounds except Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O and L-cysteine&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O, then, adjust pH to 7.5. Dispense 19 ml of medium into 50-ml vials, purge with N<sub>2</sub>-CO<sub>2</sub> (80:20) gas and fix with a stopper. After autoclaving, add filter-sterilized Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O and L-cysteine&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O solution to each vial as reducing agents.       <br>
